From fb5ac40c82cb24db5781eec9a490bc7d9dfd1033 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 06:46:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban sync: push before pulling, bound each pull,
 one puller per board, alarm on outbox age

laptop-1 2026-11-12 (t_01a1d36ddcea59fe): after ~10 h asleep the live cursor was ~75k changes
behind. pull() read until more=false and a round pushed only after its pulls, so 1747 local edits
(oldest 9 h, attempts=0) never left the outbox; the Board kept MacBook cards scheduled.

- A round now sends (push + resolve_rejections) before its pulls as well as after. The pre-pull
  send stops at the first task_runs row: run rows are last-write-wins on the Board, and a pending
  startup sent before the pull could overwrite an end the Board already holds.
- pull() reads at most PULL_PAGE_BUDGET (20) pages per database per round and returns Pulled
  (an int with .more/.busy). A round ending its budget still repairs, refreshes remote parents,
  pushes, resolves and reevaluates; the loop reruns that board without the poll wait.
  lag.pull_done/mark_pulled are stamped only when the pull reached the feed head.
- One replica puller per board per host: _pull_replica takes board_sync_lock without waiting and
  returns busy instead of pulling (sync diff compares the replica as-is; reconcile refuses).
- dispatch_tick: its live pull holds the same lock (skipped while a round holds it), and a pull
  that runs out of its 2 s budget keeps its pages and still reevaluates on a fresh budget, so
  worker-first cards are reserved while a backlog drains.
- Detection: `sync status` prints oldest_pending_age_s; the sync loop WARNs when an unanswered op
  is older than 10 min after a good round; the dispatcher tick files one card per incident.
- publish_pickup_if_changed moved to kanban_sync_pickup_publish (re-exported) for the file cap.
